I *don't* like doing that because it is boring.  But you should definately
pick up stuff that could cause you serious harm (e.g. don't leave a wand of
death for a hill orc to zap at you).  Experience will teach you what not to
leave lying around.  I learned from elora that "broom closets" are  good
places to keep a stash.  I periodically go back to one and dump everything I
don't want to carry around with me.  Then just lock the door.  It's unlikely
that monsters will open the door, the only thing you have to worry about is
something spawning in the room ... scrolls of scare monster or Elbereth
engraving help here too.

Here's what I like to carry in my exposed inventory:

Worn armor only
Primary and secondary weapon
quick use rings (conflict, regen)
pick-axe
1 potion of full healing
unicorn horn
blindfold
stethescope
1 each of:
wand of digging
wand of teleport
wand of <hit something from far away>

I go dump stuff at my stash whenever having everything else in my bag keeps
me too close to being burdened.  Even these infrequent trips to the stash
can be boring and dangerous (because you get careless while transporting
items through known levels), but I'm currently in my best game ever at DL 49
and it's working well for me.

I would love some feedback on this list, especially omissions or things you
guys think I shouldn't carry (because that list usually keeps me about 4
potions from being burdened)



